#: ../../source/docs/common-network.rst:137
#: 91b50ce969f44660b0cb2ee1a174a8e8
msgid "Server or Client?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-network.rst:139
#: 86ba10f3c79c421f939e4573baabb581
msgid "The choice of client or server is determined by the capabilities of the device being connected. If it is a TCP server, then ArduPilot's port should be a TCP Client. If its a UDP Client, then ArduPilot would be a UDP Server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-network.rst:141
#: 1d4eac128e8f41779f8303c30220c93e
msgid "In general if a device is a controllable object to the autopilot, it would be a server, always listening for commands (ESC, Gimbal,etc.). If a continuous data stream (like an airspeed sensor), it would probably be a client, able to send data without inquiry."
msgstr ""

